{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/927042-2ed-domination-3-behavior","id":927042,"title":"(2ed) Domination 3 behavior","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-06T07:29:05-07:00","id":927042,"title":"(2ed) Domination 3 behavior","content":"Hi, again I need your help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> This is the scenario: a PC of mine used Domination 3 (with iron edict) commanding to an agent of the special forces to find the &quot;best weapon skilled agent&quot; and organize a meeting with him for the next night.<br /> Now, I don't know exactly how this command should works and what kind of problems can lead. Can you give me some advice? Specially: how the dominated agent should answer to the normal question that his colleagues will ask to him? For example: who want to meet us and why?<br /> I mean, how a dominated person should answer to this kind of questions when not specifically instruited about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T10:08:45-07:00","id":927146,"title":"","content":"The special forces operative would probably inform the PC that Chuck Norris retired from the military too long ago and he has no means of setting up that meeting. But in all seriousness the most likely outcome would have the special forces operative probably order whichever subordinate in his unit that he personally believes fits those qualifications based on the last performance evaluation (it may or may not be true) to show up for a meeting on or near the base where civilians can go at x time (when they are both not on duty) about a secret mission of some sort then inform the PC of where and when to meet.<br /> Alternatively, if he ended one of his advanced combat training classes with his instructors on an amiable note, he may ask said instructor (if he's in town) out for a drink. Then tell the PC of the time and place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T11:03:42-07:00","id":927174,"title":"","content":"I would play it out as He needs to organize that meeting. That ( with build up to it ) is what the command really is. So however that person would normally set up meetings. He would say whatever he needed to say to get it done. So it would depend somewhat on the personality of the NPC.<br /> <br /> You have to take into account that he is mesmerized so he would be a little withdrawn. He doesnt know he is being mind controlled, but if the person he is calling is like his BFF, I would give something to notice him being a tish... off. But that could just be a bad day at work. <br /> <br /> I think the answers would be vague and it might go something like this: <br /> <br /> <br /> NPC calling Guy: I have someone here who wants to have a meeting with you based on your set of skills.<br /> Guy: Who?<br /> NPC: ( something like ) it's top secret... (or) Bob Smith. (or even the truth, if he knows it)<br /> Guy: Why?<br /> NPC: You are the best man for the job, most skilled and he is interested in hiring you for something.<br /> Guy: ( probably going to get a yes or a no here or some deeper questions )<br /> <br /> <br /> Problems: The guy could say no, then the NPC would still feel compelled to get it done and that might lead to bribes or more desperate measures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T11:10:13-07:00","id":927178,"title":"","content":"Many thanks. It is helpful<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}